msgid "Install packages and plugins"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Install community packages and plugins, use what they add to a study, "
"enable and remove them.*"
msgstr ""

msgid "EMStudio grows in two ways, and one page of the Settings holds both."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A **community package** carries data only: vocabularies, properties for a"
" kind of study, extractors and sets of canonical points to place on a "
"model, ways to combine them, a recording sheet, colour schemes. Every "
"tool of the Extended Matrix reads it, and it runs no code."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A **plugin** carries Python code: commands, importers and exporters, "
"checks, panels. A Python plugin has the powers of your user on this "
"computer, so EMStudio shows what it asks before installing it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A **mixed package** carries both, and you can take its data alone. "
"Extensions are installed on the computer, not in a study, and EM Tools in"
" Blender uses the same ones. A study declares the community packages it "
"uses, as it declares its vocabularies."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extensions are not the **Third-party tools**, the page below them in "
"the Settings: those are programs made by others that EMStudio calls to "
"prepare 3D models (gltfpack, Obj2Tiles, Blender…), and they add no "
"vocabulary and no command of the EM language (see "
":doc:`/reference/settings`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Open the page"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open **Settings…** (:kbd:`⌘,` on macOS, :kbd:`Ctrl+,` on Windows and "
"Linux) and choose **Extensions** in the column on the left, in the group "
"it makes with **Third-party tools**. The command search (:kbd:`F3`) finds"
" **Extensions…**, which opens the Settings on this page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Desktop"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The page lists the extensions of this computer and what the repositories "
"you use offer, and installs from disk or from a repository."
msgstr ""

msgid "Web"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Served by a StratiGraph node, the page lists the packages that the node's"
" administrator installed, and nothing is installed from the page. Their "
"properties, sheets and vocabularies reach your study all the same. "
"Packages and plugins of your own are installed in the desktop "
"application."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read the page"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Settings, the Extensions page: the official repository in the selector, "
"the filters, and the row of Geofisica opened, installed from the official"
" repository: What it contains lists its four colour ramps with their "
"stops, Where you will find it has Show me on every line."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The head of the page gives the title, the **selector of the "
"repositories** and **Install from disk…**. The selector shows the address"
" of the repository in use, the official one always first, marked "
"**official**, and **+ N more** for the others; it opens the panel "
"**Repositories** (see :doc:`repositories-signatures-updates`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Under it, **Search extensions** finds by name and by line; **All**, "
"**Installed** and **Updates** choose what is shown, and the chips "
"**Data**, **Code** and **Data + code** keep one kind."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extensions are grouped by the repository they come from (for the "
"official one, **OFFICIAL REPOSITORY**, with its key and the time it was "
"checked), then **On this computer** for those installed from disk. What a"
" repository offers and this computer does not have is a row of the same "
"list, marked **Not installed**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each row is one line: the name, the version, the kind (**Data**, "
"**Code**, **Data + code**), **used by this file** when the open study "
"declares it, the line that says what it is, its maintainer and its "
"weight. On the right, the true state of the extension and **one** action,"
" in ochre:"
msgstr ""

msgid "State"
msgstr ""

msgid "Action"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Not installed**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Install**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Installed**"
msgstr ""

msgid "—"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Data installed · code not installed**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Install the code…**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Installed · code switched off**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Enable**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Update 0.1.0 → 0.2.0**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Update**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Installed · a code update is waiting**, **Installed · a requirement is "
"missing**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The triangle on the left opens the row. A row that asks something (not "
"installed, its code missing or off, an update) opens by itself, and so "
"does the only row of the list."
msgstr ""

msgid "What it contains"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The left half of an opened row says what the extension carries, part by "
"part."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Data**: its licence, **reads in every tool**, its versions, the "
"vocabularies by name with **Vocabularies…** to open them (see "
":doc:`vocabularies`), the profile and its colour schemes, and the "
"recording sheets, offered in the **Sheets** workspace when they are "
"verified (see :doc:`/how-to/sheets/fill-the-recording-sheet`). A "
"profile's colours are of two kinds:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"a **colour scheme** of a property (*Colour scheme «…» (material)*): a "
"colour for each value, with **Into the file**, which copies it into the "
"open study, where the **Colours** window lists it under *In the file* "
"(see :doc:`/how-to/space/colours-and-legend`);"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"a **colour ramp** (*Colour ramp «Viridis» (5 stops)*): colours along a "
"range of values, the colours of a plugin's slices. Geofisica brings four,"
" *Grey*, *Viridis*, *Hot (amplitude)* and *Jet (resistivity)*; you choose"
" one in the extension's panel (**Colours**), not in the study's colour "
"schemes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Code**: its licence, Python, the programs it runs in (EMStudio, "
"Blender), what it brings counted (for example *8 commands, 1 reader, 1 "
"panel, 1 Space layer, 3 Space tools, 1 Inspector section*), its versions,"
" whether it is verified, whether it is enabled, and the key that signed "
"it. Verified has two steps: the **signature** (these are the bytes its "
"repository published) and a **review** (someone named has read this "
"code). A code with both is marked **reviewed by … on …**; a code signed "
"and not yet reviewed says so with the step that is missing, *from "
"extendedmatrix, signed ✓ · one step missing: a review of its code*; a "
"code from disk, or from an unsigned repository, says **not verified** "
"(see :doc:`repositories-signatures-updates`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Asks to**: each permission, with the reason the plugin gives."
msgstr ""

msgid "A ● marks a part on this computer, a ○ a part that is not."
msgstr ""

msgid "Where you will find it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The right half says where each thing the extension brings shows in "
"EMStudio, one line per place: **File ▸ Bring in…** (a reader, and whether"
" it reads a folder), **Space ▸ sidebar (N) ▸ tab «…»** (the tab of its "
"panels, named as the extension unless they name one; or **A window of its"
" own**), **Space ▸ Layers**, **Space ▸ toolbar (T)**, **Inspector** (a "
"section, and the kind of node it reads), **File ▸ Import** and **File ▸ "
"Export**, **Command search (F3) · Preferences ▸ Extensions** (a command "
"of the plugin that no menu draws), **A node's context menu**, **Checks**,"
" **Tabular ▸ Columns**, **Status bar**, **Narrative ▸ Export**, "
"**Vocabularies** (in the Inspector's pickers), and **Python**, the line "
"that runs a command from the console. For a command of the plugin, **Show"
" me** opens the command search with the commands of that extension."
msgstr ""

msgid "**●** — it is there now."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**○** — it appears once the code is installed (or loaded: enabled, or "
"after EMStudio restarts)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The places are known before the code is installed: they are read from "
"what the package declares, in the preview of an archive or in the archive"
" it came from, and nothing is written to read them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Show me**, on each line marked ●, closes the Settings, brings the right"
" workspace to the front and opens the place, lit for a moment by a ring "
"in the accent colour (a still ring when the system asks for reduced "
"motion):"
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "Line"
msgstr "Linia"

msgid "Show me"
msgstr ""

msgid "**File ▸ Bring in…**, **Import**, **Export**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the **File** menu opens with the entry lit."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Space ▸ sidebar (N) ▸ tab «…»**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the **Space**, its sidebar on the extension's tab, the panel lit."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Space ▸ Layers**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the same tab, the panel and the layer's row in the Space's Outliner lit "
"(once the study has a stack of its kind)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Space ▸ toolbar (T)**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the toolbar shown, the extension's tools lit."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Inspector**"
msgstr "**Inspektor**"

msgid ""
"a node the section reads is selected (the one selected, else one the "
"extension made) and the Inspector scrolls to the section. With no such "
"node in the study, one line says which kind of node it needs."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Vocabularies**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"a property whose values they give is selected and **Link to a "
"vocabulary** opens with their terms. With no such property, the "
"**Vocabularies** window opens and one line says why."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Python**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the **Scripting** workspace, its console with the line written, not run."
msgstr ""

msgid "At the foot"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The bar at the foot counts the repositories in use, the extensions and "
"the updates, and offers **Update all (…)** when there are updates, "
"**Clean up…**, **Folders** (the folders of this computer, when the "
"pointer rests on it) and **How to build an extension**, which opens the "
"guide :doc:`/extending/index`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Install from disk"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On the page, press **Install from disk…** for a ``.zip`` archive (or drop"
" the archive on the page). On the desktop, **Install from a folder…** "
"takes a package's folder, the one that holds its ``em-extension.toml``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EMStudio reads the archive without writing anything and opens **Install "
"an extension**. The head gives the name, the version and where it comes "
"from, here **from disk**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The panel **Data** lists the vocabularies the package brings, each with "
"its licence and tier, and what it adds: properties, extractors, sets of "
"canonical points, combiners, sheets, colour schemes. It ends with **No "
"code: read by every tool**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The panel **Code**, for a plugin, is marked **NOT VERIFIED, from disk**. "
"It lists **Permissions, and why:** (each permission with the reason the "
"plugin gives), **It can:** (for example *read the graph*, *write the "
"graph*), **It appears in:** (for example *File ▸ Import*, *the context "
"menu of a node*), and the sentence **A Python plugin has your user's "
"powers on this machine.**"
msgstr ""

msgid "Answer with one of the buttons:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Install everything**: the data and the code, for a mixed package;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Data only**: the vocabularies and the data, no code on this computer; "
"the row then says **Data installed · code not installed**, and **Install "
"the code…** adds it later;"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Install**: for a package that carries one kind only;"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Cancel**: nothing is installed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The answer is your trust in the code. The question is asked again only "
"when a new version changes what the plugin asks, what it can do or where "
"it comes from; otherwise the panel says that permissions, capabilities "
"and source are the same as the last trust, and no new question is asked. "
"A code that a repository lists as reviewed is marked with who read it and"
" when (see :doc:`repositories-signatures-updates`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use a package in a study"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A study declares the community packages it uses, with their version. When"
" you open a study that declares a package this computer does not have, a "
"message says **This file uses packages not installed here**, with "
"**Extensions…**: the page lists them at the top. The study opens all the "
"same, and its values keep their labels; install the package to read its "
"properties and sheets."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a newer version of a declared package is installed here, the page "
"says that the file uses an older version, and offers **Update the "
"declaration to …**. For a version that may change the meaning of the "
"data, **What changes…** shows the package's notes first, and **Keep the "
"old one** leaves the file as it is. A new declaration is saved with the "
"file and the message that confirms it offers **Undo**."
msgstr ""

msgid "Place a package's points on a model"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extractors and the sets of canonical points of a package become tools"
" of the **Viewer & card** when it shows a document's 3D model. They "
"appear in the Viewer's bar after its own six tools, in the group **Tools "
"of the community packages**; the tooltip of each gives its name, its "
"package, what it places (a point, a line of two points, a path, a closed "
"surface) and how many clicks it takes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose an extractor's tool and click on the model as many times as the "
"tool says. The extractor enters the graph, with its value, as one step of"
" ``Edit ▸ Undo``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A set of canonical points (the tool marked ⁘) is placed with a guided "
"pose. A row appears under the tools: **Unit**, the unit whose surface is "
"read (the selected one, or the one the model is tied to); **Point**, the "
"point the next click places (✓ placed, \\* required); **Skip**; **⇋**, "
"the symmetric point; **Expected**; and **Compute**. The hint says **Place"
" the point:** with its name and how many are placed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click on the model for each point. After three points, **Expected** shows"
" where the others should be, as a help and never as a value; a point "
"placed far from where the others expect it is reported and kept as "
"placed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When every required point is placed, the values that the package declares"
" are computed by themselves and become properties of the unit; "
"**Compute** runs the computation at any time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The **Inspector** shows the pose: **Pose of «…»** with the points placed "
"out of the set, and the points still missing."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Placing a package's points needs the desktop application, which writes "
"them with the package's library: in the web version the tools are visible"
" but switched off, and their tooltip says so."
msgstr ""

msgid "Run a plugin's commands"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Once installed and enabled, a plugin's commands appear where the plugin "
"says, the places that **Where you will find it** lists:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the command search (``Edit ▸ Search commands…``, :kbd:`F3`): type the "
"name of the command, or of its extension;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``Settings… ▸ Extensions``, the section **Commands of the plugins** under"
" the extensions, with a section for each plugin, its name and version and"
" the mark **not verified** for a code from disk, its commands, and **Open"
" «…»** for its panels; a plugin that did not load is listed with the "
"reason;"
msgstr ""

msgid "``File ▸ Import`` and ``File ▸ Export``;"
msgstr ""

msgid "the context menu of a node in the Matrix and in the Space;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the **Warnings** sheet of the **Tabular** window, for a plugin that "
"checks the study;"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Bring in…**, for a file that only a plugin can read;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"a section of the **Inspector**, a computed column of the **Tabular** "
"window (read only), a line of the status bar, a tool of the 3D, or a "
"panel."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each change a plugin writes is one step of ``Edit ▸ Undo``, with its line"
" in the Log, and the act records in its chain which plugin made it. A "
"file that an exporter returns is saved where you choose."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The plugins of this computer run in the desktop application, through its "
"local service. The web version does not load them; inside a room it "
"offers the plugins of the node instead (see below)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable, disable and remove"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The gestures of an installed extension are at the foot of its opened row;"
" the row's one action is on its line."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Disable** keeps the plugin installed and turns its code off; the row "
"then says **Installed · code switched off**, and **Enable** turns it on "
"again."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Install the code…** adds the code to a package installed as data only. "
"It shows the panel **Code** again and asks the same question. For an "
"extension that came from a repository, the code comes from that "
"repository, checked against its index and its signature as at the first "
"installation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Remove the code** takes the code away and keeps the data: the package "
"becomes data only."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Remove the data** takes away every version of the data."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Versions…** shows the versions on this computer side by side (see :doc"
":`repositories-signatures-updates`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Remove the package** takes away code and data."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each removal says first what goes. The vocabularies a package brought "
"stay on this computer, like fonts, because a study may use them; a box, "
"unticked, offers to remove them too. For a plugin, a second unticked box "
"removes what the plugin saved on this computer (its own settings and "
"state)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Load a plugin you are writing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With the experimental functions on (``Settings… ▸ Advanced``, "
"**Experimental functions**), the page ends with the row **Development "
"folder**, marked **beta**. Open it, type or choose a folder of this "
"computer and press **Use**: the plugins in its sub-folders load where "
"they are, without installing and without the trust question, marked "
"**development, not verified**. After changing a plugin's files, press "
"**Reload** on its line. **Clear** forgets the folder."
msgstr ""

msgid "Plugins of the node, in a room"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the web version, inside a room, the page also shows **Plugins of the "
"node**: code that the node's administrator installed and that the node "
"runs for the room in a closed space, with no network, none of the node's "
"files and a time limit. The section says whether the node's isolation is "
"proved; if it is not, the plugins stay off. The owner of the room, or an "
"administrator, turns a plugin on with **on in this room**; then its "
"commands can be run from the section, and what a command writes arrives "
"as changes of the room. A command that writes is available only to those "
"who can write in the room."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extensions installed once on this computer and shared with EM Tools: "
"packages whose properties, sheets, colours and tools serve every study "
"that declares them, and plugins whose commands take their place in the "
"menus, each act recorded with the plugin that made it."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`repositories-signatures-updates`, to install from a repository and "
"keep extensions up to date."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`vocabularies`, for the vocabularies a package brings."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`python-console`, to run Python on the open study."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/explanation/extensions-and-trust`, for what a package, a plugin "
"and the trust question are."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/reference/windows`, *Plugin panel*."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/reference/desktop-and-web`."
msgstr ""

